  "25710312": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "pearls-debrief"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "Eppich and Cheng's 2015 paper is the original description of PEARLS (Promoting Excellence And Reflective Learning in Simulation), a blended debriefing framework that deliberately combines three distinct facilitation strategies - learner self-assessment first, then a facilitated focused discussion, and only then directive feedback or teaching where a knowledge gap remains. The framework includes a scripted debriefing tool specifically so facilitators new to debriefing have concrete language to fall back on, rather than needing to improvise a structured conversation from scratch. SafeFlow's structured-debrief prompts follow this same self-assessment-first, teach-last sequence, on the basis that a debrief which starts by telling people what went wrong teaches less than one that starts by asking them."
  },
