  "31698289": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "pace-ladder"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "PACE itself (Probe-Alert-Challenge-Emergency) is Clinical Human Factors Group training material rather than a peer-reviewed paper, so this record links the closest matching primary research instead: a 2019 qualitative study of a graded-assertiveness communication module taught to first-year nursing students before their first clinical placement. Students and staff reported that rehearsing an escalating framework for \"speaking up\" in a low-stakes classroom setting built confidence and a sense of permission to advocate, well before they faced a real ward hierarchy under pressure. This supports SafeFlow's own graded-ladder design: giving reviewers scripted, escalating language for raising a concern is a rehearsal aid, not just a reminder that they are allowed to speak up."
  },
