  "35776738": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "sepsis-screen"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "This systematic review of nurses' knowledge, attitudes and practice around sepsis found generally adequate knowledge but persistent misconceptions, including the belief that sepsis is simply inevitable in critically ill patients, alongside low confidence in promptly recognising and escalating it. Barriers reported spanned individual, patient, physician and system levels, and the review found education, simulation, and structured screening tools were the main interventions shown to help. SafeFlow's sepsis-screen prompts are designed in that spirit - as a structured aid rather than a substitute for clinical judgement."
  },
