  "41446475": {
    "cueTypes": [
      "discharge"
    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "This UK quality improvement project on a respiratory ward found that a structured weekend continuity checklist cut missed blood-test handovers from 20% to 2% and took discharge-summary completion from 55% to 100% across two Plan-Do-Study-Act cycles. It is a small single-ward study, but it shows how a simple structured tool can close specific, recurring discharge and handover gaps around reduced-staffing periods. SafeFlow's discharge cue reflects the same underlying risk: continuity information is most likely to be dropped exactly when staffing is thinnest."
  },
