    ],
    "verification": "abstract-read",
    "safeflowSummary": "This 2026 systematic review of fifteen studies on SBAR and ISBAR-based handover tools found they were generally associated with improved communication, safer patient transfers and fewer reported adverse events, with structured training improving adherence. Findings were mixed in some complex or context-specific settings, so the review describes only a moderate level of certainty in the evidence rather than a guaranteed fix. SafeFlow treats structured handover prompts the same way - a support for consistent communication, not a guarantee against every gap."
  },
